{"slug": "cabbage-caesar-salad", "nyt_id": 782914412, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/782914412-cabbage-caesar-salad", "name": "Cabbage Caesar Salad", "author": "Melissa Clark", "description": "Substituting juicy, crunchy shredded cabbage for the usual romaine adds texture and sweetness to Caesar salad. You can even make it a few hours in advance (store it in the fridge until serving). The cabbage does get a bit softer as it sits, but a rest lets the flavors meld. Tearing the bread into croutons gives more texture to the dish because of the ragged edges, which turn nice and crisp in the oven. For a vegetarian version, substitute capers for anchovies and use vegan Worcestershire sauce or coconut amino acids.", "servings": {"text": "6-8 servings", "min": 6, "max": 8, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": 10, "cook_minutes": 20, "total_minutes": 30, "raw": {"total": "30 min", "prep": "PT0H10M", "cook": "PT0H20M"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "1 small baguette or chunk of sourdough bread (about 8 ounces), preferably day-old, torn or cut into bite-size pieces (about 4 cups)", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "small baguette or chunk of sourdough bread (about 8 ounces)", "preparation": "preferably day-old, torn or cut into bite-size pieces (about 4 cups)", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "½ cup extra-virgin olive oil, divided", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "extra-virgin olive oil", "preparation": "divided", "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "½ cup grated Parmesan, divided, more for garnish", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "grated parmesan", "preparation": "divided, more for garnish", "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "Salt and pepper", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt and pepper", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "2 tablespoons fresh lemon juice, more to taste", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "fresh lemon juice", "preparation": "more to taste", "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "4 anchovy fillets (or 1 teaspoon drained capers)", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "anchovy fillets (or 1 teaspoon drained capers)", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "1 fat garlic clove, finely grated or minced", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "fat garlic clove", "preparation": "finely grated or minced", "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "1 teaspoon Dijon mustard", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "dijon mustard", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "½ teaspoon Worcestershire sauce (or coconut aminos)", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "worcestershire sauce (or coconut aminos)", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "¼ cup mayonnaise", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "mayonnaise", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "8 cups shredded cabbage or coleslaw mix (24 ounces)", "group": null, "quantity": 8.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "shredded cabbage or coleslaw mix (24 ounces)", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Make the croutons: Heat oven to 400 degrees. On a rimmed sheet pan, toss bread pieces with 3 tablespoons olive oil and 3 tablespoons cheese to coat evenly. Spread in an even layer, sprinkle lightly with salt and bake until crunchy and evenly browned, 10 to 15 minutes, tossing halfway through. Taste a crouton and add more salt if needed. Use a spatula to scrape up any crunchy cheese stuck to the pan and stir into the warm croutons. Let croutons cool on the baking pan."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Meanwhile, make the dressing: In a blender or using an immersion blender, combine the lemon juice, anchovies, garlic, mustard, Worcestershire sauce and a pinch each salt and pepper, and pulse a few times to break up the anchovies."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Add the mayonnaise and the remaining 5 tablespoons olive oil, and blend until smooth. Taste and add more lemon juice, salt and pepper as needed."}, {"position": 4, "text": "In a large bowl, combine the cabbage, croutons, remaining 5 tablespoons cheese and enough of the dressing to coat the cabbage. Toss well, adding more dressing as needed. Top with more cheese and pepper, and serve."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 311.5, "protein_g": 8.2, "carbohydrates_g": 20.7, "fat_g": 22.4, "saturated_fat_g": 4.3, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, "cholesterol_mg": 10.8, "sodium_mg": 422.7, "fiber_g": 2.9, "sugar_g": 4.2, "unsaturated_fat_g": 17.3, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["american"], "diet": ["alcohol-free", "peanut-free", "pork-free", "sesame-free", "shellfish-free", "soy-free", "tree nut-free"], "course": ["main course", "side dish"], "meal": ["lunch", "dinner"], "occasion": [], "other": ["baguette", "sourdough", "parmesan", "anchovy", "caper", "dijon mustard", "cabbage", "slaws", "bake", "easy", "make-ahead", "weeknight"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/07/01/multimedia/01FD-APPE-CAESARREX-MC-Cabbage-Caesar-1-gpjb/01FD-APPE-CAESARREX-MC-Cabbage-Caesar-1-gpjb-facebookJumbo.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": true}], "rating": {"average": 5.0, "count": 724}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2026-07-01", "scraped_at": "2026-09-06T22:26:45.563357+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
